    "n": 2,
    "mode": "native",
    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-magenta);\" data-correct=\"A\" data-multi=\"\" data-rationale=\"S3 presigned URLs grant temporary access to private objects without requiring the requester to have AWS credentials. The URL includes a signature and expiration time. After expiration the URL is no longer valid. The SDK generates the URL using the credentials of the IAM principal making the request.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;Question 1: a download link that expires in 15 minutes&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;Generate an S3 presigned URL for the object using the AWS SDK. Set the expiration to 15 minutes. Provide the presigned URL to the user.&quot;, &quot;Configure the S3 bucket policy to allow public read access. Generate a URL with a custom expiration parameter. Validate the parameter in a Lambda@Edge function.&quot;, &quot;Create temporary IAM credentials using AWS STS for each download request. Provide the credentials to the user to access S3 directly.&quot;, &quot;Configure S3 Object Lock with a 15-minute retention period. Generate a standard S3 URL for the object.&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;Generate an S3 presigned URL for the object using the AWS SDK. Set the expiration to 15 minutes. Provide the presigned URL to the user.&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;S3 presigned URLs grant temporary access to private objects without requiring the requester to have AWS credentials. The URL includes a signature and expiration time. After expiration the URL is no longer valid. The SDK generates the URL using the credentials of the IAM principal making the request.&quot;, &quot;explanations&quot;: {&quot;A&quot;: &quot;S3 presigned URLs grant temporary access to private objects without requiring the requester to have AWS credentials. The URL includes a signature and expiration time. After expiration the URL is no longer valid. The SDK generates the URL using the credentials of the IAM principal making the request.&quot;, &quot;B&quot;: &quot;Making the bucket publicly readable exposes all documents to anyone with the URL, regardless of expiration. Custom expiration parameters in URLs are not natively enforced by S3. A Lambda@Edge function adds complexity and does not provide the same security as built-in presigned URL enforcement.&quot;, &quot;C&quot;: &quot;Issuing temporary IAM credentials to end users requires them to make authenticated AWS API calls. This adds complexity to the client application and requires the user to understand AWS authentication. Presigned URLs are simpler because they work as standard HTTP GET requests.&quot;, &quot;D&quot;: &quot;S3 Object Lock prevents objects from being deleted or overwritten for a specified retention period. It does not control read access or provide time-limited download links. Object Lock is a data protection feature, not an access control mechanism for temporary sharing.&quot;}, &quot;sources&quot;: [&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/using-presigned-url.html&quot;, &quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-java/latest/developer-guide/examples-s3-presign.html&quot;]}\" data-sources=\"[&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/using-presigned-url.html&quot;, &quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-java/latest/developer-guide/examples-s3-presign.html&quot;]\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 5 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 1 of 7</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">click an option</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">Question 1: a download link that expires in 15 minutes</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Generate an S3 presigned URL for the object using the AWS SDK. Set the expiration to 15 minutes. Provide the presigned URL to the user.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Configure the S3 bucket policy to allow public read access. Generate a URL with a custom expiration parameter. Validate the parameter in a Lambda@Edge function.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Create temporary IAM credentials using AWS STS for each download request. Provide the credentials to the user to access S3 directly.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Configure S3 Object Lock with a 15-minute retention period. Generate a standard S3 URL for the object.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div><div class=\"sm-check-fb\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div class=\"sm-source\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-question\"></i> Knowledge check &middot; Content Review Session 5</div></div>",
