  {
    "n": 3,
    "mode": "native",
    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-magenta);\" data-correct=\"A\" data-multi=\"\" data-rationale=\"Amazon Bedrock Guardrails provides built-in sensitive information filters that detect and redact PII in both inputs and outputs. Content filters evaluate text against predefined categories including Hate and Violence with configurable strength levels. A single guardrail configuration handles both requirements without custom code.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;Question 2: keeping account numbers out of an answer&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;Create a Bedrock guardrail with sensitive information filters configured to redact PII entities such as account numbers and social security numbers. Add content filters with HIGH strength for the Hate and Violence categories. Apply the guardrail to the Bedrock API calls.&quot;, &quot;Write a Lambda function that processes all Bedrock responses. Use regular expressions to detect and redact PII patterns. Add keyword matching for harmful content categories.&quot;, &quot;Add instructions in the system prompt directing the model to avoid outputting PII or responding to harmful content.&quot;, &quot;Configure an AWS WAF rule to inspect Bedrock API request and response payloads. Create custom rules to block PII patterns and harmful content.&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;Create a Bedrock guardrail with sensitive information filters configured to redact PII entities such as account numbers and social security numbers. Add content filters with HIGH strength for the Hate and Violence categories. Apply the guardrail to the Bedrock API calls.&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;Amazon Bedrock Guardrails provides built-in sensitive information filters that detect and redact PII in both inputs and outputs. Content filters evaluate text against predefined categories including Hate and Violence with configurable strength levels. A single guardrail configuration handles both requirements without custom code.&quot;, &quot;explanations&quot;: {&quot;A&quot;: &quot;Amazon Bedrock Guardrails provides built-in sensitive information filters that detect and redact PII in both inputs and outputs. Content filters evaluate text against predefined categories including Hate and Violence with configurable strength levels. A single guardrail configuration handles both requirements without custom code.&quot;, &quot;B&quot;: &quot;Writing custom regex patterns for PII detection requires maintaining complex pattern libraries and handling edge cases. Regex-based content filtering for hate speech and violence is unreliable compared to ML-based classifiers. Amazon Bedrock Guardrails provides these capabilities as a managed service without custom code.&quot;, &quot;C&quot;: &quot;System prompt instructions are not a reliable security control. Models can be manipulated through prompt injection to ignore system prompt restrictions. PII may still appear in responses despite instructions. Bedrock Guardrails provides deterministic enforcement that cannot be bypassed by prompt manipulation.&quot;, &quot;D&quot;: &quot;AWS WAF inspects HTTP request and response headers and bodies for web applications. WAF is designed for web application protection at the edge and is not integrated with Amazon Bedrock API calls. WAF cannot inspect the content of Bedrock model invocations or filter LLM responses.&quot;}, &quot;sources&quot;: [&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-sensitive-filters.html&quot;, &quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails.html&quot;]}\" data-sources=\"[&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-sensitive-filters.html&quot;, &quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails.html&quot;]\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 5 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 2 of 7</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">click an option</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">Question 2: keeping account numbers out of an answer</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Create a Bedrock guardrail with sensitive information filters configured to redact PII entities such as account numbers and social security numbers. Add content filters with HIGH strength for the Hate and Violence categories. Apply the guardrail to the Bedrock API calls.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Write a Lambda function that processes all Bedrock responses. Use regular expressions to detect and redact PII patterns. Add keyword matching for harmful content categories.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Add instructions in the system prompt directing the model to avoid outputting PII or responding to harmful content.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Configure an AWS WAF rule to inspect Bedrock API request and response payloads. Create custom rules to block PII patterns and harmful content.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div><div class=\"sm-check-fb\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div class=\"sm-source\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-question\"></i> Knowledge check &middot; Content Review Session 5</div></div>",
