    "n": 4,
    "mode": "native",
    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-magenta);\" data-correct=\"A\" data-multi=\"\" data-rationale=\"An interface VPC endpoint powered by AWS PrivateLink creates a private connection between the VPC and Amazon Bedrock. Traffic between the VPC and Bedrock stays within the AWS network and does not traverse the public internet. A VPC endpoint policy controls which Bedrock actions are permitted through the endpoint.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;Question 3: calling a model without touching the internet&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;Create an interface VPC endpoint for Amazon Bedrock in the VPC. Configure the endpoint with a VPC endpoint policy that allows the required Bedrock API actions. Update the application&#x27;s security group to allow outbound traffic to the endpoint.&quot;, &quot;Deploy the application in a private subnet with a NAT gateway. Configure the NAT gateway to route Bedrock API traffic through the VPC.&quot;, &quot;Configure an S3 gateway endpoint in the VPC. Store Bedrock model artifacts in S3 and invoke models through the S3 endpoint.&quot;, &quot;Enable VPC peering between the application VPC and the Amazon Bedrock service VPC. Route traffic through the peering connection.&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;Create an interface VPC endpoint for Amazon Bedrock in the VPC. Configure the endpoint with a VPC endpoint policy that allows the required Bedrock API actions. Update the application&#x27;s security group to allow outbound traffic to the endpoint.&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;An interface VPC endpoint powered by AWS PrivateLink creates a private connection between the VPC and Amazon Bedrock. Traffic between the VPC and Bedrock stays within the AWS network and does not traverse the public internet. A VPC endpoint policy controls which Bedrock actions are permitted through the endpoint.&quot;, &quot;explanations&quot;: {&quot;A&quot;: &quot;An interface VPC endpoint powered by AWS PrivateLink creates a private connection between the VPC and Amazon Bedrock. Traffic between the VPC and Bedrock stays within the AWS network and does not traverse the public internet. A VPC endpoint policy controls which Bedrock actions are permitted through the endpoint.&quot;, &quot;B&quot;: &quot;A NAT gateway allows resources in private subnets to access the internet for outbound connections. Traffic through a NAT gateway still traverses the public internet to reach AWS service endpoints. This does not meet the requirement for traffic to remain within the VPC.&quot;, &quot;C&quot;: &quot;S3 gateway endpoints provide private access to Amazon S3 only. Amazon Bedrock is a separate service with its own API endpoints. You cannot invoke Bedrock models through an S3 endpoint. Bedrock requires an interface VPC endpoint (PrivateLink) for private connectivity.&quot;, &quot;D&quot;: &quot;VPC peering connects two VPCs directly but is used between customer VPCs or between accounts. Amazon Bedrock does not expose a customer-peerable VPC. AWS PrivateLink (interface VPC endpoints) is the mechanism for private connectivity to AWS managed services like Bedrock.&quot;}, &quot;sources&quot;: [&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/vpc-interface-endpoints.html&quot;]}\" data-sources=\"[&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/vpc-interface-endpoints.html&quot;]\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 5 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 3 of 7</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">click an option</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">Question 3: calling a model without touching the internet</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Create an interface VPC endpoint for Amazon Bedrock in the VPC. Configure the endpoint with a VPC endpoint policy that allows the required Bedrock API actions. Update the application&#x27;s security group to allow outbound traffic to the endpoint.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Deploy the application in a private subnet with a NAT gateway. Configure the NAT gateway to route Bedrock API traffic through the VPC.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Configure an S3 gateway endpoint in the VPC. Store Bedrock model artifacts in S3 and invoke models through the S3 endpoint.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Enable VPC peering between the application VPC and the Amazon Bedrock service VPC. Route traffic through the peering connection.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div><div class=\"sm-check-fb\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div class=\"sm-source\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-question\"></i> Knowledge check &middot; Content Review Session 5</div></div>",
