  {
    "n": 6,
    "mode": "native",
    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-magenta);\" data-correct=\"A,B\" data-multi=\"1\" data-rationale=\"Action group permissions controls which tools an agent can call and under what conditions. By restricting tool access based on user permissions, the developer ensures the agent cannot perform unauthorized actions. This enforces least privilege at the agent-tool boundary.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;Question 5: an agent that can move money&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;Configure action group permissions in the agent definition to restrict which tools the agent can invoke based on the user&#x27;s permissions and context.&quot;, &quot;Implement a human-in-the-loop approval flow that pauses agent execution and requires explicit confirmation before the refund tool executes.&quot;, &quot;Add a system prompt instruction directing the agent to request user confirmation before initiating refund transactions.&quot;, &quot;Deploy the agent behind an API Gateway with a usage plan that limits the number of refund API calls per minute.&quot;, &quot;Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms to notify the security team when the agent invokes the refund tool more than five times per hour.&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;Configure action group permissions in the agent definition to restrict which tools the agent can invoke based on the user&#x27;s permissions and context.; Implement a human-in-the-loop approval flow that pauses agent execution and requires explicit confirmation before the refund tool executes.&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;Action group permissions controls which tools an agent can call and under what conditions. By restricting tool access based on user permissions, the developer ensures the agent cannot perform unauthorized actions. This enforces least privilege at the agent-tool boundary.&quot;, &quot;explanations&quot;: {&quot;A&quot;: &quot;Action group permissions controls which tools an agent can call and under what conditions. By restricting tool access based on user permissions, the developer ensures the agent cannot perform unauthorized actions. This enforces least privilege at the agent-tool boundary.&quot;, &quot;B&quot;: &quot;A human-in-the-loop approval flow intercepts sensitive actions before they execute. When the agent attempts to call the refund tool, execution pauses until a human reviewer approves or rejects the action. This meets the requirement for human approval on financial transactions.&quot;, &quot;C&quot;: &quot;System prompt instructions can be overridden through prompt injection or manipulation. Relying on prompt instructions for security controls is not reliable because the model may not consistently follow them. Deterministic approval flows provide stronger security guarantees than prompt-based controls.&quot;, &quot;D&quot;: &quot;Rate limiting through API Gateway usage plans controls the volume of requests but does not provide human approval for individual transactions. A rate limit of one refund per minute still allows unauthorized refunds to execute without human review. Rate limiting is a throttling control, not an authorization control.&quot;, &quot;E&quot;: &quot;CloudWatch alarms provide monitoring and alerting after actions have already occurred. They do not prevent or require approval before an action executes. By the time the alarm triggers, the unauthorized refund has already been processed. This is a detective control, not a preventive control.&quot;}, &quot;sources&quot;: [&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/agents-userconfirmation.html&quot;, &quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/action-handle.html&quot;]}\" data-sources=\"[&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/agents-userconfirmation.html&quot;, &quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/action-handle.html&quot;]\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 5 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 5 of 7</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">select all that apply</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">Question 5: an agent that can move money</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Configure action group permissions in the agent definition to restrict which tools the agent can invoke based on the user&#x27;s permissions and context.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Implement a human-in-the-loop approval flow that pauses agent execution and requires explicit confirmation before the refund tool executes.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Add a system prompt instruction directing the agent to request user confirmation before initiating refund transactions.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Deploy the agent behind an API Gateway with a usage plan that limits the number of refund API calls per minute.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"E\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">E</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms to notify the security team when the agent invokes the refund tool more than five times per hour.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div><div class=\"sm-check-submit\"><button class=\"sm-submit\" type=\"button\" disabled>Submit</button></div><div class=\"sm-check-fb\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div class=\"sm-source\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-question\"></i> Knowledge check &middot; Content Review Session 5</div></div>",
