  {
    "n": 7,
    "mode": "native",
    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-magenta);\" data-correct=\"B\" data-multi=\"\" data-rationale=\"Access to a foundation model must be requested in Amazon Bedrock before the model can be invoked, and the grant applies per account and per Region. IAM permission alone is not sufficient, which is why the calls fail while the role allows the action.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;Question 6: a model call that fails in a new account&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;Attach a resource-based policy to the foundation model that grants the role permission to call it.&quot;, &quot;Request access to the foundation model in Amazon Bedrock for the Region that the application uses.&quot;, &quot;Purchase provisioned throughput for the foundation model so that the application can call it.&quot;, &quot;Add the bedrock:ListFoundationModels action to the role so that the role can call the model.&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;Request access to the foundation model in Amazon Bedrock for the Region that the application uses.&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;Access to a foundation model must be requested in Amazon Bedrock before the model can be invoked, and the grant applies per account and per Region. IAM permission alone is not sufficient, which is why the calls fail while the role allows the action.&quot;, &quot;explanations&quot;: {&quot;A&quot;: &quot;Foundation models in Amazon Bedrock do not take resource-based policies, so there is nothing to attach. Access is controlled by the model access grant together with IAM identity-based permissions.&quot;, &quot;B&quot;: &quot;Access to a foundation model must be requested in Amazon Bedrock before the model can be invoked, and the grant applies per account and per Region. IAM permission alone is not sufficient, which is why the calls fail while the role allows the action.&quot;, &quot;C&quot;: &quot;Provisioned throughput reserves capacity for a model to support a required request rate. It is a capacity option for a model the account can already use, and it does not grant access.&quot;, &quot;D&quot;: &quot;The bedrock:ListFoundationModels action permits listing the available models. It does not permit invoking one, and the role already allows bedrock:InvokeModel, so this changes nothing.&quot;}, &quot;sources&quot;: [&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-access.html&quot;]}\" data-sources=\"[&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-access.html&quot;]\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 5 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 6 of 7</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">click an option</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">Question 6: a model call that fails in a new account</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Attach a resource-based policy to the foundation model that grants the role permission to call it.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Request access to the foundation model in Amazon Bedrock for the Region that the application uses.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Purchase provisioned throughput for the foundation model so that the application can call it.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Add the bedrock:ListFoundationModels action to the role so that the role can call the model.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div><div class=\"sm-check-fb\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div class=\"sm-source\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-question\"></i> Knowledge check &middot; Content Review Session 5</div></div>",
