    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-magenta);\" data-correct=\"A\" data-multi=\"\" data-rationale=\"Model invocation logging records the request and response data that passes through the service, so any personal data in a prompt is captured. Removing or masking the data in the application before the call means it is never sent and therefore never written to the logs, and logging stays enabled.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;Question 7: personal data reaching the invocation log&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;Remove the personal data from the prompt in the application before the prompt is sent to the model.&quot;, &quot;Encrypt the log destination with an AWS KMS customer managed key and restrict access to the key.&quot;, &quot;Change the invocation logging destination from Amazon CloudWatch Logs to an Amazon S3 bucket.&quot;, &quot;Apply a policy to the log destination that grants read access only to the compliance team role.&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;Remove the personal data from the prompt in the application before the prompt is sent to the model.&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;Model invocation logging records the request and response data that passes through the service, so any personal data in a prompt is captured. Removing or masking the data in the application before the call means it is never sent and therefore never written to the logs, and logging stays enabled.&quot;, &quot;explanations&quot;: {&quot;A&quot;: &quot;Model invocation logging records the request and response data that passes through the service, so any personal data in a prompt is captured. Removing or masking the data in the application before the call means it is never sent and therefore never written to the logs, and logging stays enabled.&quot;, &quot;B&quot;: &quot;Encrypting the destination protects the logs at rest and limits who can read them. The personal data is still recorded in the log content, so the requirement that it not be stored is not met.&quot;, &quot;C&quot;: &quot;The destination determines where the log data is delivered, not what the log data contains. The same prompt content, including the personal data, is written to either destination.&quot;, &quot;D&quot;: &quot;Restricting read access controls who can view the logs. The personal data remains stored in them, so this addresses access rather than the requirement that the data not be stored.&quot;}, &quot;sources&quot;: [&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-invocation-logging.html&quot;]}\" data-sources=\"[&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-invocation-logging.html&quot;]\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 5 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 7 of 7</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">click an option</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">Question 7: personal data reaching the invocation log</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Remove the personal data from the prompt in the application before the prompt is sent to the model.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Encrypt the log destination with an AWS KMS customer managed key and restrict access to the key.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Change the invocation logging destination from Amazon CloudWatch Logs to an Amazon S3 bucket.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Apply a policy to the log destination that grants read access only to the compliance team role.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div><div class=\"sm-check-fb\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div class=\"sm-source\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-question\"></i> Knowledge check &middot; Content Review Session 5</div></div>",
